From 6120dae0d0fd2cb283e8f91f7e2cc99d3bb6dae7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: vdn-h100 <none@local>
Date: Tue, 15 Sep 2026 10:39:04 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] vdn: load the Ulysses decoders after denoising, not
 before

At 768p on an 80 GiB card rank 0 dies and ranks 1-7 do not:

  [rank0]: torch.OutOfMemoryError: Tried to allocate 10.33 GiB.
  GPU 0 has a total capacity of 79.18 GiB of which 8.69 GiB is free.
    File "src/models/ops/fused_block.py", line 106, in fast_block_forward

The asymmetry is the decoders. install_ulysses gives every rank the same
transformer -- 55.5 GiB in fp8 at 768p -- but only the main rank loads the video
and audio VAEs, and those are ~11 GiB. That leaves rank 0 about 13 GiB for
activations where a block wants 10.33 GiB plus everything already live.

The decoders do nothing during the denoising loop, so load them when they are
first needed instead. Rank 0 then has the same headroom as every other rank.
Timed as its own `decoder_load_seconds` rather than folded into setup or decode,
so nothing is hidden by the move; `denoise_seconds` is untouched, which is what
the published comparison is measured on.

A 141 GiB H200 fits both at once, which is why upstream loads them up front.
src/inference/infer.py is single-GPU and unchanged.
---
 src/inference/infer_ulysses.py | 17 +++++++++++++----
 src/inference/render.py        | 18 ++++++++++++++++--
 2 files changed, 29 insertions(+), 6 deletions(-)

